  "generated_text": "Given:\n\\[\n\\frac{q}{r} = 9\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{s}{r} = 6\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{s}{t} = \\frac{1}{2}\n\\]\n\nWe need to find \\(\\frac{t}{q}\\).\n\nFirst, let's express \\(s\\) in terms of \\(r\\):\n\\[\ns = 6r\n\\]\n\nNext, substitute \\(s = 6r\\) into the equation \\(\\frac{s}{t} = \\frac{1}{2}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{6r}{t} = \\frac{1}{2}\n\\]\n\\[\nt = 12r\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute \\(s = 6r\\) and \\(t = 12r\\) into the equation \\(\\frac{q}{r} = 9\\):\n\\[\nq = 9r\n\\]\n\nFinally, find \\(\\frac{t}{q}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{t}{q} = \\frac{12r}{9r} = 2\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(\\frac{t}{q}\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
